# ── Change 1: bump OEM Revision (0x00000002 → 0x00000003)──────────────
# Problem: the kernel's initrd DSDT override mechanism only replaces the
#          firmware table when the override table's OEM Revision is
#          GREATER than the firmware's; otherwise it is silently ignored.
# Rationale: the kernel matches on Signature + OEMID + OEM Table ID and
#          requires oem_revision to be strictly greater than the firmware
#          table (firmware = 0x2; bump to 0x3 so the override applies).
# Source: [kernel doc initrd_table_override](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/acpi/initrd_table_override.html);
#         [Arch Wiki "DSDT"](https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/DSDT);
#         j0hnwang F27 patch "Change 1 (N)" →
#         [github.com/j0hnwang/OMEN-Transcend-16-ACPI-fix](https://github.com/j0hnwang/OMEN-Transcend-16-ACPI-fix)

@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
  *     Compiler ID      "HP  "
  *     Compiler Version 0x00040000 (262144)
  */
-DefinitionBlock ("", "DSDT", 2, "HPQOEM", "8C4D    ", 0x00000002)
+DefinitionBlock ("", "DSDT", 2, "HPQOEM", "8C4D    ", 0x00000003)
