# ── Change 2: delete the whole Device (IC04) — boot-hang root cause ───────────────
# Problem: the DSDT declares IC04 twice in the _SB.PC00 scope:
#          an integer field IC04 (64-bit) and a Device (IC04) with _HID
#          "HPIC0004" collide on the same name. When I2C4._PS3 calls
#          SOD3(IC04), the name resolves to the Device, and SOD3's
#          (GPCB() + Arg0) arithmetic treats a Device as an integer
#          → AE_AML_OPERAND_TYPE → ~50% chance of Oops/infinite loop
#          and a boot hang.
# Rationale: with the colliding Device removed, IC04 always resolves to
#          the integer field, restoring both SOD3 and I2CH(IC04). This
#          removes the root cause rather than working around a symptom.
# Source: [LauriSarap/omen-transcend-16-linux-fix](https://github.com/LauriSarap/omen-transcend-16-linux-fix) (F.25 Fix 1);
#         [j0hnwang/OMEN-Transcend-16-ACPI-fix](https://github.com/j0hnwang/OMEN-Transcend-16-ACPI-fix) "Change 2 (L)"

@@ -36967,18 +36967,6 @@ DefinitionBlock ("", "DSDT", 2, "HPQOEM", "8C4D    ", 0x00000002)
